\section{Method}
\label{sec:method}

% TODO: Full method description (pipeline overview, style-controlled rewriting, NLI gating, pairwise comparison protocol)

\subsection{Causal Framework}
\label{sec:causal_framework}

Figure~\ref{fig:dag} presents the assumed data-generating process.
Three variables govern the observed judge score $Y$: the style attribute $S$ (e.g., formality), the original content quality $Q$, and the judge's internal scoring function.
Both $S$ and $Q$ causally influence $Y$; the goal of CSD is to isolate the effect $S \to Y$ while blocking confounding through $Q$.
Style-controlled rewriting generates a text pair that differs along a single style axis, but any rewriting operation risks inadvertently altering content quality ($R \to Q$).
The NLI entailment gate approximates the \emph{do}-operator by filtering out pairs where the rewrite changed semantic content, thereby blocking the $R \to Q$ path and yielding an interventional estimate of the $S \to Y$ effect.
Our approach provides interventional rather than formal causal evidence: we do not claim that this DAG is a complete structural causal model, nor do we invoke SUTVA or consistency assumptions from the potential outcomes framework.

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\begin{tikzpicture}[
    node distance=2.2cm and 2.5cm,
    every node/.style={font=\small},
    obs/.style={draw, circle, minimum size=1cm, thick},
    mech/.style={draw, rectangle, rounded corners, minimum size=0.8cm, thick, fill=gray!10},
    gate/.style={draw, rectangle, dashed, thick, fill=blue!8, font=\footnotesize},
    arr/.style={-{Stealth[length=5pt]}, thick},
    blocked/.style={-{Stealth[length=5pt]}, thick, dashed, red!60},
  ]
  \node[obs] (S) {$S$};
  \node[obs, right=of S] (Y) {$Y$};
  \node[obs, above=1.5cm of Y] (Q) {$Q$};
  \node[mech, left=1.8cm of Q] (R) {Rewrite};
  \node[gate, below=0.4cm of R] (NLI) {NLI gate};

  \draw[arr] (S) -- node[below, font=\footnotesize] {style bias} (Y);
  \draw[arr] (Q) -- node[right, font=\footnotesize] {quality} (Y);
  \draw[arr] (R) -- node[above, font=\footnotesize] {} (S);
  \draw[blocked] (R) -- node[above, font=\footnotesize, black] {\texttimes} (Q);

  \draw[arr, gray] (NLI) -- (R);

\end{tikzpicture}
\caption{Assumed data-generating process. The rewriting mechanism $R$ targets style $S$ but may inadvertently alter content quality $Q$ (dashed red arrow). The NLI entailment gate filters pairs where $Q$ changed, approximating an intervention on $S$ alone. $Y$: judge score.}
\label{fig:dag}
\end{figure}
